.TH strncat 3 2026\-02\-25 "Linux man\-pages (未リリース)" 
.SH 名前
strncat \- append non\-null bytes from a source array to a string, and
null\-terminate the result
.SH ライブラリ
標準 C ライブラリ (\fIlibc\fP,\~\fI\-lc\fP)
.SH 書式
.nf
\fB#include <string.h>\fP
.P
\fBchar *strncat(\fPsize_t ssize;
\fB              char *restrict \fP\fIdst\fP\fB, const char \fP\fIsrc\fP\fB[restrict \fP\fIssize\fP\fB],\fP
\fB              size_t \fP\fIssize\fP\fB);\fP
.fi
.SH 説明
This function appends at most \fIssize\fP non\-null bytes from the array pointed
to by \fIsrc\fP, followed by a null character, to the end of the string pointed
to by \fIdst\fP.  \fIdst\fP must point to a string contained in a buffer that is
large enough, that is, the buffer size must be at least \fIstrlen(dst) + strnlen(src, ssize) + 1\fP.
.P
It is equivalent to
.P
.in +4n
.EX
stpcpy(mempcpy(strnul(dst), src, strnlen(src, ssize)), ""), dst
.EE
.in
.SH 返り値
\fBstrncat\fP()  returns \fIdst\fP.
.SH 属性
この節で使用されている用語の説明については、 \fBattributes\fP(7) を参照。
.TS
